[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     75[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - **Signed overflow wraps as the C build performs it.** `2147483647` (`INT_MAX`)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     76[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   ends in 7, so the loop increments past it; the C binary, built without
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     77[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   optimisation, wraps to `-2147483648`. The translation uses `wrapping_add`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     78[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   These inputs emit roughly 4.3 billion lines, so they are verified by comparing
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     79[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   a bounded stdout prefix (where the wrap is directly observable, in the first
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     80[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   two lines) plus the termination status, rather than the whole stream.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     81[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - **Non-UTF-8 arguments.** `std::env::args_os()` is used rather than `args()`,
